## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Google Meet realtime audio bridges could accept malformed base64 audio chunks from direct `googlemeet.chrome` calls or paired-node `pullAudio` responses.

Related: #106474

## Why This Change Was Made

The Google Meet audio bridge now uses one owner-local base64 validation helper before policy forwarding, node-host playback, realtime voice input, and default agent transcription input. Valid audio chunks still flow through unchanged.

## User Impact

Malformed bridge audio is rejected or treated as a transient input failure instead of being decoded into arbitrary bytes and sent to playback, realtime voice, or agent transcription providers.

## Evidence

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google-meet/src/node-invoke-policy.test.ts extensions/google-meet/node-host.test.ts extensions/google-meet/index.test.ts`: 160 tests passed.
- `node --import tsx --input-type=module -`: imported the real policy, realtime bridge, and default agent bridge modules, proving invalid direct `pushAudio` does not dispatch and invalid pulled audio does not reach either `provider.sendAudio` or `transcriptionSession.sendAudio` while valid control chunks still do.
- Actual node-host `start` command-pair proof could not run on this local machine because `BlackHole 2ch audio device not found on the node.`

```text
